<div id="2026-10-26-attention-order" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-10-26 — Attention Order panel on /planning/daily</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> Added an "Attention Order" panel to /planning/daily (main branch, port :3001) so branches and projects that need attention are not buried in the todo backlog. It lists (1) worktree branches behind main or holding unique unmerged work, (2) projects with stale open work or cross-project blockers, and (3) a stale review queue of open todos older than 180 days with Close / Suspend / Keep actions. Branches are sorted by most behind main first, then oldest last commit. The panel is placed in the Today’s Work tab alongside Cross-Project Dependencies, Application Error Audit, and HelpDesk Tickets, above Today’s Focus Queue. Each group is shown as a collapsed card inside a closed Attention Order card; clicking opens it. The list inside each card is capped at 20 items with a link to view the rest.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> Todo #2616: projects and branches were getting lost in thousands of open todos. Coordinating on main lets every worktree pick up the same attention signal after merging.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Util/AttentionOrder.pm</code> (new), <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Controller/Planning.pm</code>, <code>Comserv/root/admin/planning/DailyPlan.tt</code>, <code>Comserv/root/admin/planning/_attention_panel.tt</code> (new), <code>Comserv/root/static/css/planning/daily-plan.css</code>.</p>
</div>
